{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they brought to him yet more, etc.</b> Meaning — from things that required craftsmanship to be made with them, such as spun thread of techelet, etc., and of goat hair, and all the items that are fashioned by hand. And this is the reason for their delay, that they did not bring until after a day or two, for they were occupied and bringing their handiwork day by day. But the monetary donations, which were needed immediately, they had already brought on the first day, all at once."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:01.300658754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}